# 🐳 Global Docker Services for Development Purpose 

This setup provides globally accessible Docker containers for use across multiple projects:

- ✅ MySQL (with phpMyAdmin)
- ✅ MongoDB
- ✅ Redis

All services run inside their own folders and are connected via a shared Docker network: `global_network`.

---

## 🚀 Quick start — `services.sh`

One script installs and manages everything. From the repo root:

```bash
./services.sh                    # interactive picker: choose what to install
./services.sh up all             # start every service
./services.sh up mysql redis     # start specific ones
./services.sh status             # what's running, with ports and URLs
./services.sh down mysql         # stop a service (data volume is kept)
./services.sh restart all
./services.sh pull all           # refresh images
./services.sh logs mysql         # follow logs
./services.sh list               # available services
./services.sh --help
```

It creates the shared `global_network` for you, loads each service's `.env`,
and pulls in dependencies automatically — asking for `phpmyadmin` also starts
`mysql`, `sentry-log` also starts `postgres` and `redis`. Service names are
case-insensitive (`pgadmin` == `pgAdmin`).

---

## ⚙️ 1. Manual Setup (what the script does under the hood)

### 🔌 Create the Shared Network (only once)

```bash
docker network create global_network

🚀 Start Any Service
Each service lives in a separate folder. To start any of them:

cd ~/Docker-Services/<service-name>
docker compose --env-file .env up -d

Replace <service-name> with one of: mysql, mongodb, redis, phpmyadmin.


📄 2.env Configuration

🔸 MySQL
DB_CONNECTION=mysql
DB_HOST=mysql_global
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=your_database
DB_USERNAME=root
DB_PASSWORD=pass


🔸 MongoDB
DB_CONNECTION=mongodb
DB_HOST=mongodb_global
DB_PORT=27017
DB_DATABASE=your_database
DB_USERNAME=admin
DB_PASSWORD=adminpass


🔸 Redis
REDIS_HOST=redis_global
REDIS_PORT=6379
REDIS_PASSWORD=secretpass

# Optional
QUEUE_CONNECTION=redis
CACHE_DRIVER=redis
SESSION_DRIVER=redis


🔸RABBITMQ
QUEUE_CONNECTION=rabbitmq
RABBITMQ_HOST=rabbitmq_global
RABBITMQ_PORT=5672
RABBITMQ_USER=admin
RABBITMQ_PASSWORD=adminpass
RABBITMQ_VHOST=/



🧭 3. Access GUI Tools
🔹 phpMyAdmin
URL: http://localhost:8080
Host: mysql_global
Username: root
Password: pass



🔹 MongoDB Compass
DSN: mongodb://admin:adminpass@localhost:27017


🔹 RedisInsight
Host: localhost
Port: 6379
Password: secretpass


🌐 RabbitMQ Web UI
Once running, access the RabbitMQ Management Dashboard at:
🔗 http://localhost:15672
Username: admin
Password: adminpass
